WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.820
[Music]

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:06.240
[Teeth are to keep!]

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.720
[Produced for the Dental Health Division,
Department of National Health and Welfare

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.580
by the National Film Board of Canada]

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:20.120
[Script... P. K. Page &amp; Jim MacKay, Animation...
Jim MacKay, Ray Roy, S. D. Rigolo, Music...

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.300
Eldon Rathburn, Camera... Lyle Enright]

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:32.359
[Narrator:] One quiet summer afternoon the
whole town seemed to be asleep.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.680
[Music]

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.570
But the strangest noises are coming from the
Smiths' house. Is there something the matter

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.230
with Junior?

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:51.320
[Music]

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:58.079
Junior has cut his first tooth. His parents
are proud. Roger thinks teeth are for chewing

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:05.079
with, but you can't chew celery with only
one tooth.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.549
One tooth is like a pair of scissors with
only one blade, it won't cut.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.540
The front teeth in the top jaw and front teeth
in the bottom jaw can cut the food into little

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:23.330
pieces like a pair of scissors.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:26.360
[Scissors sound]

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.939
Back teeth are like nutcrackers, they crush
the food.

00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:34.549
[Cracking sound]

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:47.629
Like a mortar and pestle, they grind it.
But we must help our teeth to do their job
of cutting, crushing, and grinding.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:53.590
Teeth need care to keep them healthy and well
just as the body does.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.009
[Bells ringing]

00:01:56.009 --> 00:02:02.729
Teeth must be healthy to chew properly. Unhealthy
teeth are bad for the whole system.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.899
[Music]

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.380
Ginger keeps his teeth healthy.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:26.060
The Smiths help their teeth by eating raw
carrots and celery and apples and salad. Junior

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.870
does his best on a biscuit.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.560
Afterwards, Mr. Smith has some news. Tomorrow
they will go on a picnic.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:41.800
[Joyful music as the older son and the dog dance about together.]

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:50.640
Roger, in his excitement, almost forgets that
after eating, tiny bits of food remain in

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:56.910
the mouth and cause tooth decay, and though
you can't see it, the tooth rots day by day.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:02.409
But if time were speeded up, you could watch
the tooth decay.

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:12.029
[ Background noise like clock ticking very
fast ]

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:17.900
And if the holes get really big, often the
tooth must come out.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.760
[Background noise, as if a tooth is being whisked out of the mouth.]

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.670
The other teeth try to fit in the empty space
and when the teeth are in the wrong places

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.230
it's difficult to chew.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.690
[Music]

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:36.840
But Roger knows he can help cut down decay
by brushing away the small bits of food right

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:42.090
after eating. He can even brush his teeth
while thinking of the picnic and so can the

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:47.170
rest of the family.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:59.840
[Music and head images of people brushing their teeth.]

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:06.840
After they've eaten, right away they brush
their teeth to help stop decay.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.080
[Music]

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.709
After breakfast, lunch, and supper, it doesn't
take long to keep your teeth clean. It leaves

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:24.709
plenty of time to get ready for the picnic
and all the Smiths are busy.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:33.750
All except Roger, and Roger is trying to help
his teeth decay by eating candy, but Mrs. Smith

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:39.910
[swaps a sandwich?] instead, for sweets cause
decay.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:50.940
The picnic, the picnic thinks Roger as he
finishes his sandwich and goes to bed. The

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:59.210
picnic, the picnic, the picnic, um, there's
something else he should think about too.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:12.900
Ginger is trying to help him remember. Picnic...sandwich...toothbrush.
Roger remembers just in time to use his toothbrush

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:17.480
right after eating.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:31.620
[ Music ]

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:38.860
Next morning it's beautiful weather for the
picnic. The Smiths can hardly wait to start.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:50.030
But they must make one stop on the way for
the car to be checked for cars, like teeth, should always be checked before trouble begins.

00:05:58.039 --> 00:06:01.780
Now the Smiths are really on their way to
the country.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:13.820
[Car drives past a sign that reads, "Ask your
dentist about sodium fluoride."]

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.280
[ Music ]

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:24.160
And what a wonderful picnic it is.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:35.180
[Music...child and dog cavort, then join others on a picnic blanket laden with food.]

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:43.640
There's milk, there are apples and oranges,
there are brown bread sandwiches of tomatoes,

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:51.590
there are radishes, and brown bread sandwiches
of meat.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:59.610
For these are the foods, which added together,
build strong healthy teeth.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:07.100
 And because it is a picnic and they didn't bring their toothbrushes,
the Smiths rinse their mouths with water to

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:11.490
wash away the little bits of food and keep
their teeth clean.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:19.060
[Image of teeth and bubbles accompanied by scrubbing, bubbling sounds]

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:26.360
After lunch, the Smiths all do the things they like to do in the fresh air and sun. [Father is shown fishing]

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:35.820
[Music..little girl plays, mother is reading, baby is sleeping]

00:07:35.849 --> 00:07:42.849
Roger likes exploring.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:53.020
[ Music...Roger and the dog play in the woods]

00:07:55.539 --> 00:08:00.669
Following Ginger, he meets a man sitting under
a tree. He's a very nice man and he throws

00:08:00.669 --> 00:08:05.149
sticks for Ginger to fetch.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:14.000
 And he picks a
four-leaf clover and gives it to Roger for luck.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:19.560
But just at that moment a storm comes up.

00:08:19.569 --> 00:08:24.489
[Sound of thunder and ominous-looking sky.]

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:31.480
The Smiths pack their things and get ready
to go. They all begin to shout for Roger.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:45.490
Why doesn't he hurry, where can he be? Here
he comes, running as fast as he can.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:56.120
Next morning at breakfast, Roger is thinking
about the man and the picnic, so he's not

00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:00.440
very interested when his mother reminds him
that this is the day he is going to the dentist.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:06.370
Birthday once a year, dentist twice a year.
He'll have his teeth checked in advance just

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:09.310
as they check the car at the garage.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.430
He doesn't really want to go, he'd sooner
play with Ginger.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:17.690
[Doorbell to dentist's office ringing.]

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:24.680
But a big surprise is in store for him. He
finds that the dentist is his very good friend

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:30.080
who gave him the four-leaf clover and there
is hardly anything the matter with his teeth,

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:35.589
for Roger keeps them in good condition by
following four good rules.

00:09:35.589 --> 00:09:42.589
He helps to prevent decay by using his toothbrush
right after eating. He eats the food that

00:09:42.589 --> 00:09:48.589
builds strong teeth. It's as easy as two and
two.

00:09:48.589 --> 00:09:55.589
He avoids too much candy, especially between
meals, because sweets can cause decay. 

00:09:55.830 --> 00:10:01.910
And to make sure his teeth are healthy and strong,
he visits the dentist twice a year. 

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.740
Four rules, like the four-leaf clover.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:13.620
[The End, Produced by the National Film Board
of Canada, MCMXLIX.]

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:16.140
[Teeth are to Keep, Dental Health Division
and Information Services Division, 

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:19.700
Department of National Health and Welfare Ottawa]

